# Railway upload rules. Takes precedence over .gitignore for `railway up`.
#
# The key difference from .gitignore: rootfs/system/ IS uploaded here. Those
# ~115 MB of Android runtime libraries can't live in git (proprietary, huge),
# but the wrapper container is useless without them, so they ride along in the
# build context on deploy instead.
#
# rootfs/data/ stays excluded — that's the signed-in session, and it must never
# be baked into an image. On Railway the wrapper mints its own session at
# runtime from the USERNAME/PASSWORD service variables onto a mounted volume.

rootfs/data/
downloads/
node_modules/
.git/
.claude/
*.log
.env
